{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S3 — First-class AWS Bedrock provider (native, no gateway) with measured prompt caching\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nrebar has no Bedrock path. Our clients will reach Claude through Bedrock more often than through the direct\nAnthropic API, and PR #121's answer — front Bedrock with an OpenAI-compatible gateway — forces every operator\nto stand up and accredit a proxy, and gives up prompt caching, the retrying transport, and native structured\noutput in the process.\n\n## Approach\n\nRegister a `bedrock` builder in the provider factory [rebar:7468-25e5-ae4f-43d1] that constructs pydantic-ai's\nnative `BedrockConverseModel` with a `BedrockProvider`, authenticating through the ambient AWS credential chain\n(instance role in production, `AWS_PROFILE`/env locally) — no rebar-managed key. Prompt caching is already selected by the\n`prompt_cache_style == \"bedrock\"` capability shipped in story f184, which sets **exactly two** keys —\n`bedrock_cache_instructions` and `bedrock_cache_tool_definitions`. An earlier draft of this plan named a third\n(`bedrock_cache_messages`); that is **rejected** for parity, because the direct-Anthropic path sets only the\nmatching two and `AnthropicModelSettings.anthropic_cache_messages` is likewise left unset. Enabling message\ncaching on Bedrock alone would make it cache MORE than Anthropic, which is a new behaviour with its own cost\nand TTL profile — a separate decision with its own measurement, not a third key smuggled in here. The parity\nbar in story 0d76 is measured against exactly these two keys. Ships as a new `[bedrock]` optional extra\n(`pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]`) so boto3 stays out of the default `[agents]` install; the builder raises a clear\nmissing-extra error, mirroring `runner._import_pydantic_ai`.\n\n**Caching HAS been measured (real AWS, us-east-2, account 5797…98).** The measurement is done; this section\nrecords the results and the decisions they force, so no implementer has to guess. Oracle: the same request twice\nwith a `cachePoint` after a ~4000-token stable system prefix, reading `cacheReadInputTokens` /\n`cacheWriteInputTokens` off the real Converse response.\n\n1. **On-demand model ids are not invokable at all** in this account/region — both\n   `anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` and the older `anthropic.claude-3-haiku-20240307-v1:0` return\n   `ValidationException: Invocation of model ID … with on-demand throughput isn't supported. Retry your request\n   with the ID or ARN of an inference profile.` So this story's original on-demand-vs-profile comparison is\n   moot: **only inference profiles work**, and rebar's documented default must be one.\n2. **A regional inference profile DOES cache.** `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`: attempt 1\n   `cache_write=4017, cache_read=0`; attempt 2 `cache_write=0, cache_read=4017`; reproducible across runs (a\n   later run hit a still-warm cache, 5-minute TTL). This **refutes the premise of pydantic-ai #4381** for this\n   model/region — the issue this story was built around does not reproduce.\n3. **Caching is MODEL-dependent and fails SILENTLY.** `us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-5-20251101-v1:0` and\n   `global.anthropic.claude-opus-4-5-20251101-v1:0` both report `cache_read=0` AND `cache_write=0` on both\n   attempts, billing the full 4029 input tokens every call — no error, no warning. A controlled same-model\n   comparison (`us.` vs `global.`) showed BOTH fail, so the discriminator is the **model**, not the profile\n   prefix. Silent full-price billing is the real hazard here.\n4. `us.anthropic.claude-3-haiku-20240307-v1:0` with a `cachePoint` hard-fails:\n   `AccessDeniedException: You invoked an unsupported model or your request did not allow prompt caching.`\n\n**Decision A — the default is `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`**, the verified-caching regional inference\nprofile. Config accepts any profile id; this is what the docs recommend and what the parity story measures.\n\n**Decision B — rebar must WARN when caching was requested but both counters are zero.** Because failure is\nsilent, an operator otherwise pays full input price on every call forever with no signal. This mirrors the\nexisting `_warn_if_zeroed_usage` telemetry guard: observability only, never blocking.\n\n### Decision C — `temperature` is FATAL on Bedrock for some models (found by measurement, not in the original plan)\n\n`us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7` with `temperature=0` returns **400 `ValidationException: temperature is\ndeprecated for this model`**; the identical call without it succeeds. Reproduced through pydantic-ai as well:\n`BedrockConverseModel` + `BedrockModelSettings(temperature=0.0)` → `ModelHTTPError` 400.\n\nThis breaks rebar's gates on Bedrock, not just a corner case: `runner.py` sets `model_settings[\"temperature\"]`\nwhenever `cfg.temperature`/`req.config.temperature` is set, and the plan-review **Pass-2 verifiers deliberately\nsend `temperature=0`** so re-verifying a finding does not resample. Critically,\n`_drop_unsupported_sampling_settings` exists ONLY in pydantic-ai's `models/anthropic.py`, **not** in\n`models/bedrock.py` — so the direct-Anthropic path degrades gracefully (warning: \"Sampling parameters\n['temperature'] are not supported … will be ignored\") and the Bedrock path hard-fails.\n\n**Decision: carry it as a capability, using the override mechanism story f184 already built.** Add\n`supports_temperature: bool` to `ModelCapabilities`, defaulting True, and add a rebar override entry that\nwithdraws it for the affected Bedrock models; `runner.py` omits `temperature` from `model_settings` when the\ncapability is False, logging once that it did. Rationale: f184's override table exists precisely for \"cases\nupstream gets wrong or does not cover\", this is one, and it keeps the decision in the single capability registry\ninstead of a provider-name branch. Rejected alternatives: dropping temperature on ALL Bedrock calls (loses the\ngreedy Pass-2 determinism that keeps verification stable); catching the 400 and retrying without it (burns a\nbillable multi-minute agentic call and keys on model-specific error text).\n\nNote this also widens f184's signed capability record, which story 343b stamps into the verdict sidecar — doing\nit now is cheaper than after that payload shape is signed in the field. It directly de-risks story eb6e (the\nproduction review-bot cutover with no Anthropic fallback), which would otherwise hard-fail on such a model.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** OpenAI-compatible gateway fronting Bedrock (PR #121). No proxy is needed for the\nnative path, and the gateway path measurably loses caching and native structured output.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py` (**new leaf**, mirroring `anthropic_model.py`) — the `bedrock` builder and\n  its `BedrockProvider`/`BedrockConverseModel` construction. It does NOT go in `providers.py`: that file is at\n  289 LOC against the **300-LOC cap that is an attested criterion of closed story 7468**, so the builder\n  would breach a signed criterion. `providers.py` gains only the one-line registry entry.\n- `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py` — `supports_temperature` on the record + the Bedrock override entry\n  (Decision C). The profile override for Bedrock-hosted Claude and the `prompt_cache_style == \"bedrock\"`\n  cache-settings selection are **ALREADY SHIPPED by closed story f184** — verify, do not re-add.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — omit `temperature` when the capability withdraws it. NOTE: this file is at\n  EXACTLY the 800-LOC hard cap (task 2682), so this change must be net-neutral or the split lands first.\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — Bedrock region + model-id/inference-profile config keys.\n- `pyproject.toml` — `[bedrock]` optional extra.\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — regenerated.\n- `tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py` (new); `tests/live/test_bedrock_cache.py` (new, env-gated).\n\n## Testing\n\nTwo tiers, because the mechanism spans a pure construction path and a real external service.\n\n- Unit (construction, mocked boto3 client): the builder produces a `BedrockConverseModel` whose settings carry\n  the three `bedrock_cache_*` keys; a plain on-demand id and an inference-profile ARN both construct; a missing\n  `[bedrock]` extra raises `LLMConfigError` naming the install command. Contrast case: an `anthropic` model\n  still gets `anthropic_cache_*`, never `bedrock_cache_*`.\n- Live canary (env-gated, `REBAR_LIVE_BEDROCK=1`, skipped in default CI): issue the same cached-prefix request\n  twice and assert `usage.cache_read_tokens > 0` on the second — the observable oracle for \"caching works\".\n  Run it for both the on-demand id and the inference-profile ARN and record both results.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [operator-attested] `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=bedrock:<claude-id> rebar review-plan <ticket>` completes with a valid structured verdict\n      against real Bedrock, output attached as a comment on this ticket\n- [x] **MEASURED** — the cache canary result is recorded on this ticket: on-demand ids are not invokable at all\n      here; `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` caches (`cache_write=4017` then `cache_read=4017`, reproducible);\n      `us.`/`global.` opus-4-5 silently do not cache. rebar documents `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6` as the\n      default\n- [ ] a test asserts rebar WARNS when caching was requested but both cache counters are zero (Decision B),\n      since the failure is otherwise silent and bills full input every call\n- [ ] a test asserts `temperature` is omitted for a model whose `supports_temperature` capability is False,\n      and still sent for one where it is True (Decision C) — the contrast case\n- [ ] unit tests pass with no AWS credentials present (boto3 client mocked), proving default CI is unaffected\n- [ ] `pip install nava-rebar[agents]` still installs without boto3 (`python -c \"import boto3\"` fails in that env)"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785386062009453001,"uuid":"2e3b58ed-b45e-4867-8da1-2a1f7e4657fd"}